The main problem remains open. I proved three obstructions to the proposed prescriptions:

- Twist infima give \(-4t\) for XX instead of \(A=2t\).
- Unrestricted seam twists can depend on the gauge representative.
- A canonical-gauge, uniformly gapped spin chain has a positive smooth-cutoff energy deficit of order \(1/L\), despite \(A=0\).

I also constructed a finite, gauge-invariant upper semicontinuous cutoff observable. Its comparison with physical \(A\) remains unproved, so this does not establish finite \(F(d)\). No divergent physical-\(A\) sequence was found.

All checks passed. Derivations and results are in [PROOF.md](PROOF.md) and [RESULT.md](RESULT.md); progress and local memory were updated.

